# Patterns match from the context root only, so a bare `.env` would leave
# packages/backend/.env free to reach the builder stage via
# `COPY packages/backend/`. `**/` covers every depth, the root included.
# The build reads no .env.example, so none is let back in.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.log
signal-data
.git
.github
.vscode
.claude
docs
